WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.440
Rhiannon: Mental health concerns
within the family may involve a

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:08.550
parent, a child, or a sibling or even
a grandparent, but whoever is affected,

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.860
the general effects of mental health
concerns, can have an impact on the

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.889
whole family and their relationships.

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:18.455
Knowledge that a parent is mentally ill
can be very difficult for a child or

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:22.720
young person as they may feel they are
to blame for any related behaviours.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:27.590
Leah: Having a loved one, act violently
towards someone in the family will always

00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:29.570
have a negative effect on mental health.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:33.950
Children who witness or are subject
to violence at home, are likely to

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:38.030
suffer from depression or develop
more severe mental health issues.

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:45.839
Children may also have other concerns;
they may feel they are missing out,

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:49.260
because they’re looking after a family
member and doing jobs around the

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.349
house most people their age don’t do.

00:00:52.199 --> 00:00:55.479
Some children feel ashamed about
their family member and do not

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:58.820
want to bring friends home, some
are even worried that they will

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.530
suffer from the same mental illness.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:04.389
Rhiannon: As mental illness can
often appear in someone’s teens, it

00:01:04.389 --> 00:01:07.410
is common for someone to be living
in the family home when their issues

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:11.559
become apparent, most commonly
anxiety disorders and depression.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:16.960
However, in severe cases, children or
young people may express suicidal thoughts

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.510
or attempt suicide or may use drugs or
alcohol to cope with their feelings.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:27.389
In these instances, a child’s mental
health concerns will most likely

00:01:27.389 --> 00:01:29.419
require professional help and support.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:34.020
Leah: The school environment has a
significant impact on a young person’s

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:36.550
emotional welfare and mental well-being.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:41.060
An estimated three children in every
classroom suffer from a diagnosable

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:45.450
mental health problem and there is a
general trend to increased levels of

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.540
stress and lower levels of wellbeing.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:52.050
Students with a poor standard of education
are more likely to experience mental

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:56.350
health problems, this has been attributed
to the fact that children from poorer

00:01:56.350 --> 00:02:00.339
backgrounds, often do not have access
to the best standards of teaching.

00:02:00.759 --> 00:02:03.860
Rhiannon: Some young people suffer
a lot of distress going to school

00:02:04.209 --> 00:02:09.807
it could be due to relationships
with their peers, body image,

00:02:09.807 --> 00:02:10.201
classroom anxiety or exam stress.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:13.430
and the growing number of children
and young people experiencing

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:16.770
poor mental health is one of the
biggest challenges in the classroom.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.090
Leah: Mental health problems in children
and young people cause distress and can

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:25.200
have wide-ranging effects, including
impacts on educational attainment

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:29.630
and family life and relationships,
as well as affecting physical health

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:35.790
and in severe cases, life chances.

